nss_qdisc: initialise the stats hash table lock

nss_qdisc_htable_init() allocates the table that maps a qos_tag to its
qdisc for the statistics, but never initialised the table's lock; the
structure around it comes from kzalloc(), so the lock was only ever
zeroed memory. Every NSS qdisc that is set up takes that lock
(nss_qdisc_stats_qdisc_attach() -> nss_qdisc_htable_entry_add()), and
lockdep reports it at the first one ("trying to register non-static
key", tc creating nssprio when SQM starts on IPQ5018) and turns itself
off. Initialise it with the rest of the table.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_htable.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/nss_qdisc_htable.c
@@ -221,6 +221,7 @@ bool nss_qdisc_htable_init(struct nss_qdisc_htable *nqt)
 	}
 
 	nqt->count = 0;
+	spin_lock_init(&nqt->lock);
 	nss_qdisc_htable_hlist_init(nqt->htable, NSS_QDISC_LIST_TABLE_INIT_SIZE);
 	return true;
 }
